From 365dcc85f886e23c142eefb4088c0832129350f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeff R. Day" <phroun@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:47:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] purfecterm: cap the terminal grid dimensions (degenerate-fit
 safety net)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both fit paths derive the child grid from a pixel rectangle divided by a
cell size: updateTerminalSize (cell surface) and paintGraphical (pixel
surface). A degenerate input — a near-zero cell size mid-resize, or a
size-feedback runaway between a hosted terminal and its host — drove those
divisions to hundreds of thousands of columns or rows, which the emulator
faithfully allocated one makeEmptyLine per row into a multi-gigabyte
buffer that wedged and then OOM-killed the process.

Clamp each computed dimension through clampGridDim to [0, maxTermGridDim]
(2000). No real display approaches 2000 cells in a dimension, so the cap
never touches a legitimate fit; a negative or otherwise degenerate value
collapses to 0, which the callers already treat as "no usable size" and
skip the resize. This is a backstop independent of any single runaway's
root cause.

Adds TestClampGridDim.
---
 core/version.go                             |  2 +-
 objects/trinkets/purfecterm.go              | 25 +++++++++++++++++--
 objects/trinkets/purfecterm_gfx.go          |  4 +--
 objects/trinkets/purfecterm_gridcap_test.go | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 objects/trinkets/purfecterm_gridcap_test.go

